1
00:00:00,835 --> 00:00:04,585
(Sheldon:)I don't care. There are far too many
historical anomalies for my comfort.

2
00:00:04,755 --> 00:00:06,135
Oh, okay, how about this?

3
00:00:06,298 --> 00:00:09,008
(Raj:)You can go dressed
as a Star Trek science officer...

4
00:00:09,176 --> 00:00:12,926
(Raj:)...exploring a planet similar to Earth
in the 1500s.

5
00:00:13,681 --> 00:00:14,761
(Sheldon:)You mean like Spock?

6
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:17,100
(Leonard:)Sure.

7
00:00:17,268 --> 00:00:19,768
(Sheldon:)Fascinating.

8
00:00:21,105 --> 00:00:24,445
- Hey, fellow scientists. Sheldon.
LEONARD: Mm.

9
00:00:26,944 --> 00:00:29,024
Why don't we move there
so Leslie can join us?

10
00:00:29,196 --> 00:00:30,326
Yeah, let's do it.

11
00:00:35,953 --> 00:00:38,203
(Sheldon:)If you're having trouble
deciding where to sit...

12
00:00:38,372 --> 00:00:40,122
(Sheldon:)...I suggest One Potato, Two Potato...

13
00:00:40,291 --> 00:00:44,331
(Sheldon:)...or as I call it, the Leslie Winkle
Experimental Methodology.

14
00:00:46,964 --> 00:00:49,964
- Don't make this hard for me.
- It's not hard. It's simple.

15
00:00:50,134 --> 00:00:53,174
(Sheldon:)You can either sit with me,
your friend, colleague and roommate...

16
00:00:53,345 --> 00:00:58,025
(Sheldon:)...or you can sit with an overrated scientist
you might have sex with.

